      "text": "To solve the problem, we start by using the relationships given by Vieta's formulas for the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\). According to Vieta's formulas, the roots \\(r, s, t\\) satisfy the following equations:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 20,\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 18,\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 7.\n\\]\n\nWe are asked to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\). First, we expand the expression \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\):\n\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rt + rs + rst.\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute the values from Vieta's formulas into this expression:\n\n\\[\n1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rt + rs + rst = 1 + 20 + rs + rt + st + rt + rs + rst.\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n1 + 20 + (rs + rt + st) + (rt + rs) + rst = 21 + (rs + rt + st) + 2(rs + rt + st) + 7.\n\\]\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n\\[\n21 + 3(rs + rt + st) + 7 = 28 + 3(rs + rt + st).\n\\]\n\nFrom Vieta's formulas, we know that \\(rs + rt + st = 18\\). Substituting this value in, we have:\n\n\\[\n28 + 3 \\cdot 18 = 28 + 54 = 82.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) is \\(\\boxed{82}\\).",
