      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) where \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\) are the roots of the polynomial equation \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas. Vieta's formulas relate the coefficients of the polynomial to sums and products of its roots.\n\nFor the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), the coefficients are:\n\\[a_3 = 1, \\quad a_2 = -20, \\quad a_1 = 18, \\quad a_0 = -7.\\]\n\nAccording to Vieta's formulas:\n1. The sum of the roots taken one at a time (i.e., \\(r+s+t\\)) is equal to \\(-\\frac{a_2}{a_3}\\):\n\\[r + s + t = 20.\\]\n\n2. The sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time (i.e., \\(rs + rt + st\\)) is equal to \\(\\frac{a_1}{a_3}\\):\n\\[rs + rt + st = 18.\\]\n\n3. The product of the roots (i.e., \\(rst\\)) is equal to \\(-\\frac{a_0}{a_3}\\):\n\\[rst = 7.\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\). Expanding this expression, we get:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rst.\n\\]\n\nWe already know from Vieta's formulas that:\n\\[r + s + t = 20,\\]\n\\[rs + rt + st = 18,\\]\n\\[rst = 7.\\]\n\nSubstituting these values into the expanded expression, we get:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) is \\(\\boxed{46}\\).",
