      "text": "Given the polynomial equation \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\) with roots \\(r, s, t\\), we need to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\).\n\nFirst, we start by expanding the expression \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\):\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rst.\n\\]\nWe recognize that \\(r, s, t\\) are the roots of the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\). By Vieta's formulas, we know the following relationships among the roots:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 20,\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 18,\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 7.\n\\]\nSubstituting these values into the expanded expression, we get:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + (r+s+t) + (rs+rt+st) + rst.\n\\]\nSubstituting the values \\(r+s+t = 20\\), \\(rs+rt+st = 18\\), and \\(rst = 7\\) into the equation, we have:\n\\[\n1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46.\n\\]\nThus, the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) is \\(\\boxed{46}\\).",
