      "text": "We are given that \\( r, s, \\) and \\( t \\) are the roots of the polynomial equation \\( x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0 \\). To find the value of \\( (1+r)(1+s)(1+t) \\), we start by expanding the expression:\n\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rst\n\\]\n\nFrom Vieta's formulas, we know the following relationships for the roots \\( r, s, \\) and \\( t \\) of the polynomial \\( x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0 \\):\n\n\\[\nr + s + t = 20\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 18\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 7\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these values into the expanded expression, we get:\n\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + (r+s+t) + (rs+rt+st) + rst\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the known values:\n\n\\[\n1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( (1+r)(1+s)(1+t) \\) is \\(\\boxed{46}\\).",
